---
/**
 * Privacy (Phase 5). Plain English, and only what the site actually does. Flagged
 * for the owner to review before launch: the flag is a bracketed placeholder,
 * so the placeholder gate keeps production builds from shipping until it's
 * removed. No certifications or legal compliance are claimed.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  og="privacy"
  view="about"
  title="Privacy"
  description="How the Monolith Web Studio website handles your details: the contact form, cookieless analytics, booking calls and how to ask for your details to be deleted."
>
  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="Privacy"
    title="Your details,"
    accent="in plain English."
    lead="What this site collects, where it goes, and how to ask me to delete it."
  />

  <section class="privacy" aria-label="Privacy details">
    <div class="container privacy__inner" data-reveal>
      <p class="privacy__review label">[REVIEW BEFORE LAUNCH]</p>

      <h2 class="heading">The contact form</h2>
      <p>
        When you send a project brief, what you enter (your name, email, business, phone if you give
        it, your answers and your message) is sent to me by email through Resend, an email delivery
        service. It ends up in my inbox and is used to reply to you about your project.
      </p>
      <p>
        While you fill the form in, your answers are kept in your browser’s session storage so a
        refresh doesn’t lose them. They are cleared when the brief is sent, or when you close the
        tab. If you send the form without JavaScript and something needs fixing, your answers are
        held in a cookie for up to two minutes so the form can show them again.
      </p>
      <p>
        To stop spam, the internet address your request comes from is checked against recent
        submissions. It is kept only in the server’s working memory, never written to storage, and
        isn’t included in the email.
      </p>

      <h2 class="heading">Analytics and performance</h2>
      <p>
        The site uses Vercel Web Analytics and Speed Insights, which don’t use cookies. They record
        things like which pages are visited, the referring site, the country, the kind of device and
        browser, and how quickly pages load. On top of that, the site sends a few anonymous events:
        which version of the 3D scene your device could show, how far through the home page story
        you scrolled, which “Start a project” or “Book a call” button you used, how far through the
        contact form you got and whether it was sent, and whether you turned the sound on or skipped
        the intro. None of these include anything you type.
      </p>

      <h2 class="heading">Booking a call</h2>
      <p>
        Booking a call is handled by Cal.com. Nothing from Cal.com loads until you choose “Book a
        call”, and what you enter there is covered by Cal.com’s own privacy policy.
      </p>

      <h2 class="heading">Hosting</h2>
      <p>The site is hosted by Vercel, whose servers handle every request, as any web host’s do.</p>

      <h2 class="heading">Your details, your call</h2>
      <p>To ask what I hold about you, or to have it deleted, email me at {SITE.email}.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy {
    position: relative;
    padding-block: var(--space-l) var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .privacy__inner {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-m);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .privacy__inner p {
    color: var(--ash-soft);
  }

  .privacy__inner .heading {
    margin-top: var(--space-l);
  }

  .privacy__inner .privacy__review {
    color: var(--lava-hot);
  }
</style>
